  partName: Intake Manifold
  description: The Intake Manifold is a medium-sized, elongated component situated
    at the top-center-front of the rocket engine, made of a Tuyaux material. It plays
    a crucial role in directing air and fuel into the engine's cylinders, ensuring
    a homogeneous mixture and efficient combustion. The Intake Manifold's design
    must balance the need for minimal flow restriction with the requirement for maximum
    fuel distribution uniformity, making it a complex and critical component.
